<p>Hi {{{Recovery__c.Contact_First_Name__c}}},<br />
<br />
Under the United States Department of Transport Rule on Refunds and Other Consumer Protections, passengers traveling on flights to, from, or within the United States are entitled to a refund for checked baggage fees (if not included in the original fare) if their baggage is significantly delayed.<br />
<br />
<strong>Your refund amount</strong><br />
<br />
You will receive a refund of {{{Recovery__c.Value__c}}}.<br />
<br />
Payments made to bank accounts outside of Australia will be converted into the equivalent local currency at the at the time of payment.</p>

<h3>How to organise your refund</h3>
<br />
To process your refund, you will need to provide us with your bank account details using our secure case portal. Visit <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/customer-care-feedback-form/update-customer-care-case.html">https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/customer-care-feedback-form/update-customer-care-case.html </a> to commence your refund.<br />
<br />
Please note that this payment is in addition to any other claims you may be eligible for, including in relation to delayed baggage.<br />
<br />
On behalf of the team at Qantas, we sincerely apologise for the inconvenience experienced.<br />
&nbsp;<br />
All customers will receive email notifications about the progress of the claim. If you are a Qantas Frequent Flyer member, you can conveniently track your refund via the request tracker in the Qantas app via ‘Track my cases’ in Help and Support.<br />
&nbsp;
<h3>Need help?</h3>
<br />
Call us on 13 13 13 (in Australia) or your local&nbsp;<a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us.html">Qantas Office</a> for assistance.<br />
<br />
Have your Customer care reference number {{{Recovery__c.Parent_Case__c}}} ready to enter.<br />
<br />
<strong>If you’re suspicious</strong><br />
<br />
Not sure something is genuine? Remember, Qantas will never ask you to&nbsp;email&nbsp;your bank account details,&nbsp;credit card, PIN, or passwords.<br />
For more advice and warnings on scams please visit the Qantas scam assistance page -&nbsp;<a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/scam-assistance.html">https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/scam-assistance.html</a></body>
